<!-- Forest region-of-interest scenery, centred on the world origin.
     Generated together with roi_forest.yaml, whose tree list must match it; do not
     edit by hand. (The generator, tools/gen_roi_forest.py, is in the history at the
     dev-archive tag.) Built from: size=500 m square, oak=436, pine=290,
     seed=20251007. Included by worlds/templates/base_world.sdf.j2.
     1156 grass tiles, 726 trees and 101 boundary posts, all as visuals and
     collisions of ONE static link in 'forest_scenery': as separate models the same
     scenery is far heavier to load and simulate. The axis marker stays at world
     level because it carries the world's navsat sensor.
     Declares no plane geometry and no ground plane: there is exactly one plane
     collision per world, in base_world.sdf.j2.
     The search-and-rescue sites are placed by uavsim on every run. -->
    <model name="axes">
      <static>1</static>
      <link name="link">
        <visual name="r">
          <cast_shadows>0</cast_shadows>
          <pose>5 0 0.1 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry>
